# No PII / financial data (mandatory)

Agents must **not** read, query, export, paste, or modify live **parent, staff, student, or financial** data.

## Never read or open

- `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.*` (except `.env.development.example`)
- `.vercel/` or output of `vercel env pull`
- `tmp/`, `data/`, `migration/data/`, `scripts/sales/out/`
- Any CSV/SQL/backup/roster/export file
- Downloaded CMS backups or Plaid/budget dumps

## Never run (unless Rob explicitly says **ops on prod data** in that message)

- `vercel env pull`, `vercel env ls`, or any command whose purpose is loading production secrets
- HTTP/scripts that query Wix **Students**, **Memberships**, **Payments**, **StaffRoles**, **StaffPlaidItems**, **PtoBudgetLines**, **PtoBudgetEntries**, **ExpenseReimbursements**, **ContactSubmissions**, **FamilyGuardians**, **StaffGoogleTokens**, **StaffCanvaTokens**, **NewsletterSubscribers** (live rows)
- Ops scripts: `sanitize-students-directory.mjs`, `rollover-import-grades.mjs`, `check-newsletter-roster.mjs`, `backfill-cove-square-customers.mjs`, CMS backup restore, Plaid exchange against prod
- Direct DB access (`psql`, Neon prod URL, `query_render_postgres` on production)

## Allowed without asking

- Edit **code, types, schemas, UI, tests** that describe data shapes (no live values)
- Use **fixtures/mocks** from `@/lib/fixtures` (cart, checkout quotes, Riverside-shaped roster)
- **Synthetic staging** (`shmspto.vercel.app`, local `.env.development`): fixture data only, no live Wix
- Deploy from clean worktree when ship rules say so (do not pull env into the workspace to “inspect”)
- Read **public** site content and staff **help** copy (no roster APIs)

## When debugging data issues

- Ask Rob for **counts, error text, or redacted snippets** (no emails, student names, grades, dollar amounts, tokens)
- Do not request full API responses or CSVs in chat

## Pavilion vs Stone Hill

- **Pavilion** (`commons-*`): no Stone Hill Wix/Plaid/Square prod credentials. Vanilla demo only.
- **Stone Hill** live data lives in Wix CMS and Vercel env, not in git. Agents work on code paths only.
